{"skill":{"slug":"myfeed","displayName":"My Life Feed"},"version":{"version":"2.0.1","createdAt":1771249956765,"changelog":"- Fixed a typo in the environment variable name; it is now consistently Myfeed_API_KEY in all setup instructions and usage examples.\n- Corrected example usage commands to use the proper API key environment variable casing.\n- No functional or code changes; documentation update only.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":4053,"sha256":"daff8d7686b7c370d6b6467f51abdf5b9a8d37cd7e4e326313d3b8e8306c1ec4","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"README.md","size":1990,"sha256":"26efccff95059b47e6bfd643e8f4430df1bb05c4c80e3da767485f8aa4856ffa","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1677,"sha256":"99c5bb24759465cec48b8b2fc2c869c69472ee4da22c9b03c40c676985b3ef49","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789067109794,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"57efd317a6fd7b2cd8d18df9e921d8d50bdc2592ff6cf1e708f4da6190fa1ff8","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/57efd317a6fd7b2cd8d18df9e921d8d50bdc2592ff6cf1e708f4da6190fa1ff8","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: myfeed\nVersion: 2.0.1\n\nThe skill bundle is benign. It provides instructions and examples for interacting with the MyFeed REST API using `curl` and `jq`. All API calls are directed to `https://skill.myfeed.life/api` and use the `Myfeed_API_KEY` for authentication, which is consistent with the stated purpose of managing MyFeed data. There is no evidence of intentional malicious behavior such as data exfiltration, unauthorized command execution, persistence mechanisms, or prompt injection attempts against the AI agent in `SKILL.md`.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779163944464},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":36,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":7,"checkedAt":1789067109794},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a straightforward MyFeed API helper, but users should understand that it can send real invitations and reminders to other people.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network access to the fixed MyFeed API endpoint and an API key are proportionate to the stated API-integration purpose, and the skill notes that the key provides full account access.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifact is Markdown-only with no bundled executable code, installer, dependency script, or hidden runtime component; it declares jq and Myfeed_API_KEY as requirements.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The instructions are explicit about using the MyFeed REST API and phone numbers or group IDs, but they would benefit from clearer consent and confirmation guidance before contacting other people.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"There is no local persistence, privilege escalation, service installation, or background worker, but API actions may persist in the user's MyFeed account and notify invitees.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The documented purpose is to manage MyFeed things and groups, and the capability shown is limited to curl examples for creating things, inviting friends or groups, and listing groups.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you trust MyFeed with your API key and the event, group, and phone-number data you submit. Before using friend or group invites, verify the recipient or group ID and make sure you are allowed to share that phone number and send reminders.","findings":"[SQP-2] expected: The friend and group invitation behavior is central to the skill and is disclosed, though the documentation should make the third-party notification and phone-number privacy implications more prominent.\n[E1] expected: External transmission to https://skill.myfeed.life/api is the core mechanism of the skill, not hidden exfiltration; transmitted data can include event descriptions, times, group IDs, phone numbers, and the API authorization header.\n[SQP-3] expected: The phone-number formatting instruction is part of using the invite API and is not a security concern by itself, though clearer locale/API-format guidance would reduce user mistakes.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789067109794}}}}}